{"id": "EUVD-2026-103591", "enisaUuid": "a9793edf-76a0-3064-bf79-a4d721c0080c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64/boot: Disable trapping of PMZR_EL0 writes to EL2\n\n__init_el2_fgt2() writes one mask to both HDFGRTR2_EL2 and HDFGWTR2_EL2.\nPMZR_EL0 is write-only, so its trap bit, nPMZR_EL0, exists only in\nHDFGWTR2_EL2 and is therefore never set: a PMZR_EL0 write from the host\ntraps to EL2, where the nVHE hypervisor has no handler and BUG()s. The\nkernel never writes PMZR_EL0, but kernel.perf_user_access=1 has the PMU\ndriver set PMUSERENR_EL0.UEN for a task with a user-read event, so a\nwrite from EL0 reaches the trap and takes the host down without a panic\nmessage.\n\nAccumulate the HDFGWTR2_EL2 bits separately, as __init_el2_fgt() already\ndoes for HDFGWTR_EL2, and set nPMZR_EL0 with the other FEAT_PMUv3p9\nbits.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:29", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb8c90c86441c090e9036f019cf1b4d7894a2c40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/071f51188a5d8ec10535541255587976d12fc7d8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce71865bf43f88bed9d9218e9218e537150be506", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bc6b218717b9d08f466f88209251d54bc09b207"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gfjh-3rr5-qgfr", "CVE-2026-98546"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02a384d0-2dd9-3fba-bb5c-8917b34082f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858c7bfcb35e1100b58bb63c9f562d86e09418d9 <071f51188a5d8ec10535541255587976d12fc7d8"}, {"id": "0f957bd1-8ebf-32b0-93f8-aeb831d9793b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14.4 <6.15"}, {"id": "19e80daf-a427-3f9a-99f2-8b07def23c87", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "258c0d47-4588-3501-990c-8c318068abbd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "2f516eec-3c92-345f-a127-031ec114be1c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "3a6aef26-09b9-3e77-8fc1-3906a703c0d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "882f78400322c0aec4b641a7168adad9a66bc0c2"}, {"id": "9ff920e5-31a9-3359-8a84-2a543b7061fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "b275979e-15de-3ccb-8142-2ffd43cad5f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858c7bfcb35e1100b58bb63c9f562d86e09418d9 <2bc6b218717b9d08f466f88209251d54bc09b207"}, {"id": "b54020fb-f69c-3ec8-95e3-80d8a2a344e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "858c7bfcb35e1100b58bb63c9f562d86e09418d9 <ce71865bf43f88bed9d9218e9218e537150be506"}, {"id": "bedb6f46-4ac7-3725-8b2f-c3d23fe33395", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d8a405f5-f1d9-3fa5-b643-12420f917bf4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.25 <6.12.112"}, {"id": "dd3741b9-f74a-3d48-9cee-8d1343d9bb94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "686d8f7b592f3466f44aea653c8147611b351c83 <bb8c90c86441c090e9036f019cf1b4d7894a2c40"}, {"id": "f5bddb4c-1c10-3063-bb83-4e8c849ab8bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f44d8f05-3bd8-3285-ae35-665b376cca8d", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}